# MOVEMENT IV — file 72: b81-96 = CLOSING GROUP (Bb major).
# b81-84: the CELL in Bb MAJOR in four octaves of strings (cb bb1 ... vn1
#   bb4), f, moving Bb - F - Eb - CELLcad(F->Bb); winds+horns throw
#   syncopated chords on the off-quarters (beats 2 and 4).
# b85-88: roles swapped. Winds (fl, ob+cl 8vb, fg 16vb below ob) take the
#   CELL on Gm (with f#: a shadow of home) - Cm - F - F7; strings now
#   syncopate, cresc.
# b89-92: cadence in broad accented quarter-half-quarter syncopations
#   (hemiola-like): bass eb-d-c | f | f | bb = IV - I6 - ii - V(6/4-7) - I.
# b93-96: low strings + fg hammer the CELL L5 and CELLcad under tutti
#   Bb/F7 strokes; b96 one stroke, then silence (no fermata; strict time).
# Intensity: L3 (b81) -> L4 (b85-88) -> L5 (b93-95) -> 0.

